0) WHY THIS TOPIC EXISTS IN REAL SYSTEMS
===============================================================================

Before choosing any database in HLD, interviewer is actually testing:

“Can you map DATA ACCESS PATTERN → CONSISTENCY NEEDS → SCALE MODEL?”

This topic exists because every real-world system must answer:

- Do I need strict correctness?
- Do I need flexible schema?
- Will joins dominate?
- Will writes explode to millions/sec?
- Can stale data be tolerated?
- Will cross-shard transactions happen?
- How expensive is failover?
- Is horizontal scale mandatory?

This decision directly changes architecture of:
- WhatsApp chats
- Instagram feed
- Uber trip state
- Netflix watch history
- Amazon cart
- Payment ledgers
- Google Docs collaboration
- Search indexing
- Fraud pipelines

Golden senior line:
“Database choice is not SQL vs NoSQL, it is consistency model vs access pattern vs scale tradeoff.” :contentReference[oaicite:0]{index=0}

===============================================================================
1) INTUITION
===============================================================================

Simple intuition:

SQL = data with RELATIONSHIPS + RULES
NoSQL = data with SCALE + FLEXIBILITY

Think:

SQL asks:
“How are entities related?”

NoSQL asks:
“How will this be read and scaled?”

That single line explains 80% of interview decisions.

===============================================================================
2) WHY RELATIONAL DATABASE EXISTS
===============================================================================

WHY:
Real business entities are deeply connected.

Example: Amazon
- User
- Orders
- Payments
- Shipments
- Products
- Inventory

All these have relationships.

A relational database models this naturally as tables.

Example:

USERS(user_id, name)
ORDERS(order_id, user_id)
PAYMENTS(payment_id, order_id)

This gives:
- joins
- foreign keys
- constraints
- ACID
- strong correctness
- normalized updates

Best examples:
- payments
- banking
- order management
- ticket booking
- ERP
- HRMS
- ledgers

WHY this choice:
Business correctness > raw scale.

